1
00:03:44,210 --> 00:03:50,210
Terror... that screams from the grave!

2
00:07:28,421 --> 00:07:34,421
The Undead is a horror, fantasy film directed by Roger Corman.

3
00:11:12,631 --> 00:11:18,631
Two psychics place a prostitute under hypnosis in order
to learn about her past-life experiences.

4
00:14:56,842 --> 00:15:02,842
When they unwittingly send her back in time, she finds herself in the Middle
Ages, suspected of being a witch and on the verge of being executed.

5
00:18:41,052 --> 00:18:47,052
Diana Love / Helene, played by Pamela Duncan.

6
00:22:25,263 --> 00:22:31,263
Pendragon, played by Richard Garland.

7
00:26:09,473 --> 00:26:15,473
Livia, played by Allison Hayes.

8
00:29:53,684 --> 00:29:59,684
Quintus Ratcliff, played by Val Dufour.

9
00:33:37,894 --> 00:33:43,894
Gravedigger Smolkin, played by Mel Welles.

10
00:37:22,105 --> 00:37:28,105
Meg Maud, played by Dorothy Neumann.

11
00:41:06,315 --> 00:41:12,315
The Undead is a 1957 horror film directed by Roger Corman and starring
Pamela Duncan, Allison Hayes, Richard Garland and Val Dufour.

12
00:44:50,526 --> 00:44:56,526
It also features Corman regulars Richard Devon, Dick
Miller, Mel Welles and Bruno VeSota.

13
00:48:34,736 --> 00:48:40,736
The authors' original working title was The Trance of Diana Love.

14
00:52:18,947 --> 00:52:24,947
The film  follows the story of a prostitute, Diana Love (Duncan), who is put into a hypnotic
trance by psychic Quintus (Dufour), thus causing her to regress to a previous life.

15
00:56:03,157 --> 00:56:09,157
Hayes later starred in Attack of the 50 Foot Woman (1958).

16
00:59:47,368 --> 00:59:53,368
The film was released on February 14, 1957 by American
International Pictures as a double feature with Voodoo Woman.

17
01:03:31,578 --> 01:03:37,578
The film explores themes of witch, coffin, spider, reincarnation, femme fatale.

18
01:07:15,789 --> 01:07:21,789
The tone is dark.
